\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces How many tokens an incremental parser admits, over $6{,}657$ live states on JSONSchemaBench \texttt  {medium} ($|V|=126{,}349$). The distribution is bimodal and the decade between the modes is nearly empty, which is why no single $k$ suits both. Structural positions are uniformly tight; the bimodality lives inside strings, separating a partially spelled property name, which admits a handful of continuations, from a free-form value, which admits almost the whole vocabulary.}}{12}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:legalsets}{{2}{12}{How many tokens an incremental parser admits, over $6{,}657$ live states on JSONSchemaBench \texttt {medium} ($|V|=126{,}349$). The distribution is bimodal and the decade between the modes is nearly empty, which is why no single $k$ suits both. Structural positions are uniformly tight; the bimodality lives inside strings, separating a partially spelled property name, which admits a handful of continuations, from a free-form value, which admits almost the whole vocabulary}{figure.2}{}}
